    "https://jobs.kettering.edu/postings/10147": {
      "title": "Dean, Graduate Studies &amp; Research",
      "description": "Kettering University Employment Opportunities | Dean, Graduate Studies &amp; Research Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Dean, Graduate Studies & Research Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submit (1) letter of interest fully describing qualifications and experience, with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications; (2) detailed CV; and (3) the names, email addresses, and telephone numbers of at least five professional references who may be contacted. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Dean, Graduate Studies & Research Position Class Type Regular Position Type Staff Other Position Information About Kettering: Kettering University is a national leader in experiential STEM and business education, integrating an intense academic curriculum with applied professional experience. We inspire students to realize their potential and advance their ideas by combining theory and practice better than any institution in the world. Kettering University is dedicated to achieving the extraordinary through technological innovation, leadership, and service, built on values that foster respect, integrity, creativity, collaboration, and excellence in growth, global leadership, community outreach, and an engaged community of stakeholders. Benefits: include health, dental and vision coverage; retirement benefits with up to a 9% Kettering matching contribution; life and accident insurance; tuition assistance and waiver programs; vacation and holiday pay; sick and disability pay; home purchase assistance program; recreation center membership; and many other benefits. To learn more please view the Kettering University Profile. Position Status Full-time If Part Time, hours per week Posting Text Preferred Qualifications •At least 3 years of administrative experience in higher education and/or research administration; •A record of developing new graduate programs and/or expanding existing programs; •Significant leadership experience in research and grant administration at the department level and/or higher; •Experience in working with industry partners; •Experience recruiting international graduate students. Job Specific Required Qualifications •An earned doctorate in an engineering or science field, or equivalent terminal degree; •A proven track-record of research and teaching commensurate with an appointment as a tenured full professor in one of the University’s departments; •Effective leadership, interpersonal, oral and written communications skills. •Significant experience working with graduate students and promoting graduate education; •Knowledge of funding sources and regulatory issues related to grant funding; •A proven track-record in obtaining substantial external funding to support research; •Successful experience in budget management and in planning; Posting Information Posting Number SP00476 Posting Date 02/27/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Submit (1) letter of interest fully describing qualifications and experience, with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications; (2) detailed CV; and (3) the names, email addresses, and telephone numbers of at least five professional references who may be contacted. Job Duties Job Duties Percent of total time 40 Duties Develop and grow graduate programs (on-campus, online, and BS/Masters pathways). Work with the department heads and faculty on the strategic expansion of on-campus graduate education. Develop a comprehensive recruiting plan for on-campus graduate education. Develop external sources of support for graduate students and programs. Percent of total time 30 Duties Manage development and execution of faculty research programs and compliance; (both federal and applied/company sponsored). Develop and grow external funding opportunities. Work with governmental agencies, foundations, and private sector companies to identify and develop funding opportunities. Coordinate and support institutional initiatives relating to technology transfer and intellectual property issues. Work with community leaders to identify opportunities to enhance research and development in Flint and the region. Percent of total time 15 Duties Provide leadership for research and on-campus graduate programs. Develop a strategic agenda for research and graduate programs. In collaboration with the department heads, faculty and staff, provide institutional leadership in the areas of research and graduate education. Develop and manage professional development programs and translate them into degree-seeking programs. Percent of total time 15 Duties Provide administrative supervision for the offices of sponsored research and graduate studies. Provide daily supervision of the employees for the offices of sponsored research and graduate studies. Provide budget oversight. Develop and implement policies and processes across research and graduate programs. Provide compliance oversight. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you currently hold an earned Ph.D? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Kettering University, 1700 University Ave. Flint, MI 48504 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.kettering.edu/postings/10136": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor/Teaching Assistant Professor/Assistant Professor of the Practice",
      "description": "Kettering University Employment Opportunities | Tenure Track Assistant Professor/Teaching Assistant Professor/Assistant Professor of the Practice Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Tenure Track Assistant Professor/Teaching Assistant Professor/Assistant Professor of the Practice Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The position is open until filled; however, priority consideration will be given to applications received by March 30. Posting Details Position Information Classification Title Faculty Job Title Tenure Track Assistant Professor/Teaching Assistant Professor/Assistant Professor of the Practice Position Number Position Class Type Regular Position Type Faculty FLSA Exempt Other Position Information About Kettering: Kettering University is a national leader in experiential STEM and business education, integrating an intense academic curriculum with applied professional experience. We inspire students to realize their potential and advance their ideas by combining theory and practice better than any institution in the world. Kettering University is dedicated to achieving the extraordinary through technological innovation, leadership, and service, built on values that foster respect, integrity, creativity, collaboration, and excellence in growth, global leadership, community outreach, and an engaged community of stakeholders. Benefits: include health, dental and vision coverage; retirement benefits with up to a 9% Kettering matching contribution; life and accident insurance; tuition assistance and waiver programs; vacation and holiday pay; sick and disability pay; home purchase assistance program; recreation center membership; and many other benefits. To learn more please view the Kettering University Profile. Position Status Full-time If Part Time, hours per week Posting Text Preferred Qualifications -Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level; -Demonstrated excellence in research and other scholarly activity; -Experience in teaching mechatronics, dynamic systems, vibrations, and controls. Job Specific Required Qualifications -Ph.D. in Mechanical, Electrical, or Aerospace Engineering or closely related field; - ABD with completion by time of appointment will be considered; -Ability to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in dynamic systems, mechatronics; - Ability to complement at least one of our existing strengths such as advanced mobility, autonomous systems, new energy, crash safety, or related areas; -Ability to use modern engineering tools for teaching and research; -Ability to develop an externally funded applied-research program; -Demonstrated written and oral communication skills in the English language; -Ability and desire to contribute through department, university, community and professional service work. Evidence of, research for Assistant/Associate Professor and/or industrial applications of mechatronics and dynamic systems for Professor of the Practice. Note the Assistant/Associate Professor are tenure track while the Teaching Professor and Professor of the Practice are non-tenured renewable positions with the possibility of multi-year contracts. Understand and have a commitment to Kettering University Values a. RESPECT : for teamwork, honesty, encouragement, diversity partnerships with students. b. INTEGRITY : including accountability, transparency and ethics. c. CREATIVITY : fostering flexibility and innovation. d. COLLABORATION : across disciplines and with all partners. e. EXCELLENCE : in all we do. Posting Information Posting Number FP00100 Posting Date 02/19/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants The position is open until filled; however, priority consideration will be given to applications received by March 30. Job Duties Job Duties Percent of total time 45 Duties Teaching and learning duties, including course, laboratories, and curriculum development, student projects, professional development aiming at enhancing student learning and best practices in teaching and learning. Percent of total time 35 Duties Research and scholarship: This includes establishing a research program appropriate for Kettering University, and aligned with teacher-scholar model. Also, it is expected that faculty involve students in research projects, publish their research and scholarship work in peer reviewed journals, as well as presentations in conferences. Percent of total time 20 Duties Service and citizenship: This includes service activities within the department, the institution, the profession, and the community. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you authorized to work in the United States? Yes No * How many years of teaching experience do you have? None 1-3 years 4-6 years 6-10 years > 10 years * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status by Kettering University (e.g., H-1B visa status)? (Open Ended Question) * How much industry experience do you have, if any? 0-2 years 3-5 years 5-10 years More than 10 years * What do you consider to be your primary area of mechanical engineering in terms of teaching (Dynamic Systems (including courses in dynamics, modeling, mechatronics, and controls), Energy Systems (including fluid mechanics, thermodynamics, and heat transfer), or Mechanics (including statics, machine design, and solid mechanics)? (Open Ended Question) * What do you consider to be your primary area of mechanical engineering in terms of research(Dynamic Systems (including courses in dynamics, modeling, mechatronics, and controls), Energy Systems (including fluid mechanics, thermodynamics, and heat transfer), or Mechanics (including statics, machine design, and solid mechanics). (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Curriculum Vitae List of References Research Philosophy Optional Documents Kettering University, 1700 University Ave. Flint, MI 48504 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.kettering.edu/postings/10116": {
      "title": "Program Director, Graduate Studies",
      "description": "Kettering University Employment Opportunities | Program Director, Graduate Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Program Director, Graduate Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Program Director, Graduate Studies Position Class Type Regular Position Type Professional Other Position Information About Kettering: Kettering University is a national leader in experiential STEM and business education, integrating an intense academic curriculum with applied professional experience. We inspire students to realize their potential and advance their ideas by combining theory and practice better than any institution in the world. Kettering University is dedicated to achieving the extraordinary through technological innovation, leadership, and service, built on values that foster respect, integrity, creativity, collaboration, and excellence in growth, global leadership, community outreach, and an engaged community of stakeholders. Benefits: include health, dental and vision coverage; retirement benefits with up to a 9% Kettering matching contribution; life and accident insurance; tuition assistance and waiver programs; vacation and holiday pay; sick and disability pay; home purchase assistance program; recreation center membership; and many other benefits. To learn more please view the Kettering University Profile. Position Status Full-time If Part Time, hours per week Posting Text Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. or Ed.D. At least 10 years experience in High Education At least 5 years specifically responsible for Corporate Training Job Specific Required Qualifications At least 10 years experience in Higher Education Minimum of a Masters degree At least 5 years administrative experience Experience managing and completing projects Qualified candidate will be experienced in and capable of coordinating between corporate partners and the College of Engineering and Computer Science & the School of Management to create, establish, and deliver programs that are mutually beneficial; as well as grow the online graduate student population. Understanding and commitment to Kettering University Values: a. RESPECT : for teamwork, honesty, encouragement, diversity, partnerships with students. b. INTEGRITY : including accountability, transparency and ethics. c. CREATIVITY : fostering flexibility and innovation. d. COLLABORATION : across disciplines and with all partners. e. EXCELLENCE : in all we do. Posting Information Posting Number SP00474 Posting Date 02/19/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Job Duties Job Duties Percent of total time 35 Duties Initiate relationships and opportunities for Corporate Training with various businesses and organizations in cooperation with the Dean of Graduate Studies and Research. Coordinate with appropriate individuals within the University to ensure successful completion and launch of all projects. Percent of total time 15 Duties Responsible for all academic proposal development for the purposes of approval through the Academic approval process. Coordinate with appropriate individuals within the University to ensure successful completion and launch of all projects. Percent of total time 35 Duties Support Kettering University’s graduate programs with special projects including goals and initiatives by providing implementation support. Comply with timelines to ensure established guidelines. Coordinate with appropriate individuals within the University to ensure successful completion and launch of all projects. Percent of total time 15 Duties Support the advising of graduate students to facilitate high levels of customer service. Make recommendations to streamline processes to create Leaner operations. Conduct research on strategic initiatives. Identify necessary resources of special projects. Coordinate with appropriate individuals within the University to ensure successful completion and launch of all projects. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please provide the specific name of the publication or website where you learned about this posting. (Open Ended Question) * Detail in 3-4 sentences a summary of Corporate Training experience including 1-2 specific Corporate Training relationships and revenue outcome. (Open Ended Question) * Provide a 5-6 sentence paragraph with specific examples of your ability to work independently with little supervision. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Kettering University, 1700 University Ave. Flint, MI 48504 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.kettering.edu/postings/10048": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Kettering University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates should submit an application including a CV, cover letter, and list of references. The cover letter should describe relevant experience and include a summary of courses that they would be interested in teaching. A listing of currently offered courses can be found at https://catalog.kettering.edu/coursesaz/ . Proposals for new elective courses in the fields described above are being accepted. Candidates proposing new courses should include a one-page description of their proposed course. This document may be included in the Applicant Documents section marked as \"Other Document.\" Applications will be reviewed on a continuous basis. Applicants who are available to commute to our Flint, Michigan campus will be given full consideration for these positions. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Faculty Position Class Type Casual Position Type Casual Other Position Information Kettering University is seeking Adjunct Faculty to support undergraduate and graduate degree programs. Opportunities exist in the following discipline areas: • Business • Chemistry • Chemical Engineering • Computer Science • Electrical Engineering • Liberal Studies • Industrial Engineering • Mechanical Engineering • Mathematics • Technology Management • Innovation & Entrepreneurship About Kettering: Kettering University is a national leader in experiential STEM and business education, integrating an intense academic curriculum with applied professional experience. We inspire students to realize their potential and advance their ideas by combining theory and practice better than any institution in the world. Kettering University is dedicated to achieving the extraordinary through technological innovation, leadership, and service, built on values that foster respect, integrity, creativity, collaboration, and excellence in growth, global leadership, community outreach, and an engaged community of stakeholders. To learn more please view the Kettering University Profile. To apply: https://jobs.kettering.edu/postings/6196 Position Status Part-time If Part Time, hours per week Posting Text Preferred Qualifications - Job Specific Required Qualifications Qualified candidates would preferably hold a Ph.D. in their discipline, but candidates with a Master’s degree and significant industry or teaching experience will also be considered. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage and inspire students is required. Candidates with executive level industry experience are highly desired for positions within the School of Management. Adjunct faculty for courses offered at Flint campus are primarily needed during normal business hours, but opportunities for evening courses do exist. All courses may be delivered in one of three modes: Face-to-Face, virtual, or hybrid (combination of F2F and virtual). Understand and have a commitment to Kettering University Values a. RESPECT : for teamwork, honesty, encouragement, diversity partnerships with students. b. INTEGRITY : including accountability, transparency and ethics. c. CREATIVITY : fostering flexibility and innovation. d. COLLABORATION : across disciplines and with all partners. e. EXCELLENCE : in all we do. Posting Information Posting Number CP00012 Posting Date 12/12/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates should submit an application including a CV, cover letter, and list of references. The cover letter should describe relevant experience and include a summary of courses that they would be interested in teaching. A listing of currently offered courses can be found at https://catalog.kettering.edu/coursesaz/ . Proposals for new elective courses in the fields described above are being accepted. Candidates proposing new courses should include a one-page description of their proposed course. This document may be included in the Applicant Documents section marked as “Other Document.” Applications will be reviewed on a continuous basis. Applicants who are available to commute to our Flint, Michigan campus will be given full consideration for these positions. Job Duties Job Duties Percent of total time 100 Duties Class/lab preparation Class/lab presentation Develop lesson plans, and instructional materials that align with departmental learning outcomes Hold office hours/assistance to students seeking help Active involvement in departmental meetings and institutional events Evaluation of graded assignments *Assessment Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you authorized to work in the United States? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status by Kettering University (e.g., H-1B visa status)? (Open Ended Question) * Describe your college teaching experience including specific courses and duration. (Open Ended Question) * Please provide the specific name of the publication or website where you learned about this posting. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents List of References Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document Teaching Philosophy Research Philosophy Kettering University, 1700 University Ave. Flint, MI 48504 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
